Under the proposed Pharmaceutical Society of Sri Lanka (Incorporation) law, the Society may acquire and hold “any property, movable or immovable” received by “purchase, grant, gift, testamentary disposition or otherwise,” and may “sell, mortgage, lease, exchange, or otherwise dispose of” it, subject to the Act and its rules [047/2026 §13]. It may also:

- “purchase, rent construct, renovate and otherwise obtain lands or buildings” and “deal with or dispose of” them as the Council determines [047/2026 §6(a)];
- “invest any funds that are not immediately required… in such manner as the Council may determine” [047/2026 §6(e)];
- “undertake, accept, execute, perform and administer any lawful trust… or any real or personal property” [047/2026 §6(f)].

The Gazette version is identical [041/2026 §13; 041/2026 §6].
